{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "d3f006fd-b18b-5d4b-9ef9-1dd19653a4a5",
  "Description": "Renders NanoVDB liquid, smoke and fire inside a glass box.\n\nThe shader traverses the NanoVDB tree uploaded by [VolumeToNanoVdb] directly on the GPU. The liquid grid is shaded as a reflective surface; the smoke and fire grids use the depth below their zero level as density and temperature, broken up by procedural noise. Place the op inside a camera such as [OrbitCamera] and render it into a texture.\n\nAKA: NanoVDB raymarch, volume render, fluid box\n\nTips\n- Connect all three grid inputs; use LiquidAmount, SmokeDensity and FireIntensity at 0 to hide one of them.\n- Grids are rebuilt on the CPU, so keep voxel sizes moderate for animated volumes.",
  "InputUis": [
    {
      "InputId": "74e636af-eec7-51a4-89a6-bb851f98938f",
      "Position": {
        "X": 0.0,
        "Y": 0.0
      },
      "Description": "NanoVDB level set of the liquid. Connect the ShaderResourceView output of [VolumeToNanoVdb]. All three grid inputs must be connected so the shader registers stay in order; use the amount inputs to switch one off."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "5b6564b0-a48e-53c7-ae8a-ed1f362aa26d",
      "Position": {
        "X": 0.0,
        "Y": 40.0
      },
      "Description": "NanoVDB level set whose inside is rendered as smoke density."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "0f98affe-42d1-5d56-98ba-ed5bdd948ced",
      "Position": {
        "X": 0.0,
        "Y": 80.0
      },
      "Description": "NanoVDB level set whose inside is rendered as hot, emissive fire."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "cd5b7c56-40b8-5f45-b736-e2448a20af1a",
      "Position": {
        "X": 0.0,
        "Y": 120.0
      },
      "Description": "Lower corner of the glass box in world space. Rays are clipped to the box."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "c722d77b-1aca-5bf9-a22a-255b6feb87ab",
      "Position": {
        "X": 0.0,
        "Y": 160.0
      },
